{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0125","billNumberShort":"H.B. 125","billNumberLong":"HB0125S03","fileNumber":"2026FL0546","shortTitle":"Department of Natural Resources Related Modifications Amendments","currentSubVersion":"3","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"SHIPPRP","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shipp, Rex P.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"HINKIDP","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Hinkins, David P.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses provisions related to the Department of Natural Resources and related regulated areas.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>removes language related to determining the work period for certain Department of Natural Resources' employees;<hr><ltbullet>defines terms, including defining \"invasive mussel\";<hr><ltbullet>exempts an owner or operator of certain vessels from requirements related to invasive species and launching or operating the vessel on waters of the state;<hr><ltbullet>addresses vessels owned by government agencies;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to a required aquatic invasive species education course;<hr><ltbullet>addresses vessels rented or leased from a boat livery, including modifying recordkeeping requirements for a boat livery;<hr><ltbullet>modifies provisions related to collection of annual aquatic invasive species fees, including repealing outdated language;<hr><ltbullet>addresses responsibilities of the Division of Law Enforcement and the Division of Wildlife Resources;<hr><ltbullet>modifies provisions related to records kept by the Division of Water Rights, including to allow for the records to be kept in physical or electronic form;<hr><ltbullet>corrects citations;<hr><ltbullet>addresses funding of litigation;<hr><ltbullet>addresses treatment of water rights after termination or noncompliance of certain royalty contracts or mineral leases;<hr><ltbullet>removes a cap on low-interest loans related to secondary water metering;<hr><ltbullet>modifies when certain applications may be filed with the state engineer under instream flow provisions;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies rulemaking authority related to rules enforced by the Division of Law Enforcement;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the duties of the Utah Geological Survey;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the makeup of the Board of the Utah Geological Survey;<hr><ltbullet>changes the term \"buffalo\" to \"bison\" in certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>repeals the section specifying funding sources of the Watershed Restoration Initiative;<hr><ltbullet>repeals the Alternative Energy Development Tax Credit Act; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming amendments.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Patricia Owen","fiscalAnalyst":"Ivan D. Djambov","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"VHMEEYQPKV","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-02 15:14:44.063","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-02 15:14:44.063","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0125","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2026-01-02 15:14:45.890","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for HB0125","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2026-01-02 15:14:45.890","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"de